  "worked_solution": "From the graph, we see that\n\n- The slope of the tangent at $x=-3$ is negative, so ${f}^{′}(-3)<0.$\n\n- The slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is positive, so ${f}^{′}(1)>0.$\n\n- The slope of the tangent at $x=3$ is zero, so ${f}^{′}(3)=0.$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{′}(-3)<{f}^{′}(3)<{f}^{′}(1).$",
